.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Data and model artifacts
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
models/checkpoints/*
outputs/*
data/ci_claims.db
uploads-ci/
backend/data/*
backend/uploads-ci/
backend/uploads/*
.local-data/

# Per-user runtime state (repo-root RAG workspace). Never commit these:
# policies/ holds the documents people upload (their own contracts) plus the
# vector index built from them, and claims/ holds claim records and the
# LangGraph checkpoint DB. In a real deployment both are customer PII; here
# they are regenerable test state, and the binary DBs would produce
# unreadable diffs either way.
data/claim_pipeline/
data/user_policies/

# Same regenerable runtime state, but under the backend app's own copy of
# the RAG pipeline (backend/app/rag_scripts/) -- ensure_all_seeded_policies_
# ingested() rebuilds claim_pipeline/ from the committed policy PDFs on
# first app startup (a fresh random collection ID every time), and
# claims/checkpoints.sqlite is the LangGraph checkpoint DB for locally-run
# claims. Neither is reproducible source data, so neither belongs in git.
#
# backend/app/rag_scripts/data/chroma_db/ (singular, top-level -- distinct
# from claim_pipeline/policies/chroma_db/ above) is deliberately NOT
# ignored: per backend/app/rag_scripts/README.md it is the prebuilt
# 185-chunk index checked in on purpose as "the retrieval-quality
# regression bed" the RAG evaluation scripts run against. rag_outputs/ is
# likewise kept: those are the committed evaluation results (ragas_eval.json,
# chunk corpus, sweep results) this repo's reproducibility claims depend on.
backend/app/rag_scripts/data/claim_pipeline/
backend/app/rag_scripts/data/claims/checkpoints.sqlite
backend/app/rag_scripts/data/user_policies/chroma_db/

# Output of .github/scripts/generate_evaluation_results.py (the Model
# Evaluation workflow) -- a generated artifact, not source.
/evaluation-results.json

# Keep folder placeholders (do NOT ignore .gitkeep -- its only purpose is to
# be committed so an otherwise-empty directory survives in git)
